Status / Hints / TODO list for MacOS builds

- Requirements:
  - system installs:
    - need full xcode; command line tools is not enough (for qtbase)
  - Required tools not in MacOS (or not in a usable version)
    We take these from homebrew, ATM. Some bits have hardcoded paths
    to /opt/homebrew (TODO).
      - cmake
      - gnu-tar
      - gnu-sed
      - meson (not in macos)
      - bison (version in macos is too old)
  - Required libs neither in MacOS nor our current build scripts. We
    probably want to build those, ourselves, mid term (TODO)
    - boost (for libkleo)

- Setup:
  - We cannot run MacOS as a docker guest, so need a different setup.
    For now we just bypass that (internal --nodocker option), but that's
    just a temporary hack. We probably want to run in a VM.
    https://github.com/s-u/macosvm looks like a good candidate that supports
    MacOS arm64 on arm64, and is geared towards builder scenarios.
  - At a minimum, we should gather non-system build-deps in a ro volume
  - To set up /build and /src, need to modify /etc/synthetic.conf:
    - /build -> point builddir arg
    - /src -> point to repo
    - sudo /System/Library/Filesystems/apfs.fs/Contents/Resources/apfs.util -t
  - some package builds fail due to case insensitive filesytem (kdsingleapplication is the first)
    -> build filesystem needs to be on an ADFSX volume
      - sudo diskutil apfs addVolume disk3 APFSX VOLUMENAME
        (assuming disk3 is the root disk)

- Running:
  ./build.sh --mac --builddir=/Some/casesensitive/Volume

- Further TODO:
  - There is no bundling at all, yet (macdeployqt? Take code from KDE craft?)
  - There is not codesigning at all, yet
  - Test patch to find gpgconf.ctl, and provide that
